WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.420
Evidently, Tom Holland's a superhero on and
off the big screen.

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.380
A new piece published by The Hollywood Reporter
claims that Holland — who has played the

00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:13.360
friendly neighborhood hero Spider-Man since
2016's Captain America: Civil War — sprung

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.950
into action and carried out some last-minute,
heroic deeds to help bring Spidey back into

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.720
the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:24.320
In late August 2019, the web-crawler was forced
to swing out of Marvel's movie world when

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.269
it was announced that Marvel Studios and Sony
Pictures couldn't come to an agreement on

00:00:28.269 --> 00:00:32.610
how to establish new terms of the deal that
allowed Holland's Spider-Man to appear in

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:33.460
the MCU.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:37.700
Several weeks later, the two studios confirmed
that they returned to the negotiating table

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:42.260
and finally came up with a way to make everyone
happy: Marvel Studios president Kevin Feige

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:46.660
will produce a third Spider-Man movie starring
Holland, Marvel's parent company Disney will

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:51.160
receive 25 percent of the profits from said
threequel, and Spider-Man will appear in at

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:52.969
least one more MCU movie.

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:55.100
Cue the collective sigh of relief.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.420
It looks like that doozy of a cliffhanger
will pay off, after all!

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:02.780
"Spider-Man's name… is Peter Parker!"

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.640
"What the f—"

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:09.280
Striking the right revenue split apparently
played a huge part in getting Marvel, Disney,

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.009
and Sony executives back on the same page
regarding their respective involvement in

00:01:13.009 --> 00:01:14.680
the Spider-Man film series.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:19.520
What was also a major deciding factor in sealing
the new Spidey deal was Holland himself.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:24.580
According to sources close to THR, Holland,
quote, "made multiple appeals" to Walt Disney

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:30.510
Company CEO Bob Iger and contacted Sony Pictures
chairman Tom Rothman on numerous occasions

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:33.990
to help facilitate a reconciliation between
the two parties.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:38.640
The fact that Holland is set to star in another
Sony project — the forthcoming film adaptation

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.980
of the Uncharted video game series — probably
didn't hurt.

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:46.040
It was certainly admirable of Holland to get
in touch with Iger and Rothman and assist

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.960
in bringing the two opposing studios to a
resolution.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.860
It's also very much something Spider-Man would
do: a scrappy, somewhat unlikely hero pulling

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:55.960
himself out of the rubble to do the right
thing.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:02:00.540
As heart-warming and heroic as Holland's reported
appeals were, however, they aren't surprising

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:04.580
when taking a look at how he responded to
the Sony-Marvel split in the first place.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:10.060
The first time Holland spoke about Spider-Man
leaving the MCU was during D23 Expo on Saturday,

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:13.660
August 24 — several days after the shocking
news dropped.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:18.620
Holland's silence — and his alarmingly nonchalant
behavior on social media — was cause for

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:19.360
concern.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.620
Finally, when he piped up, he said exactly
the right thing.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:23.680
He told fans:

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:27.910
"It's been a crazy week, but I want you to
know I am grateful from the bottom of my heart,

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.880
and I love you 3,000."

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:34.000
As time went on and Marvel and Sony showed
no signs of getting back together for another

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.640
Spider-Man flick, Holland maintained a diplomatic,
optimistic attitude that never wavered.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:43.260
He refused to align himself with one studio
over the other — even with millions of fans

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:46.560
pulling him in different directions — and
held his head high.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:51.260
The 23-year-old actor noted that Marvel helped
make his dreams come true, and that he had,

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:55.450
quote, "five amazing years" working under
the House of Heroes, but knew that the future

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:59.960
of Spider-Man would be, quote, "equally as
awesome and amazing" and that Sony would,

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.280
quote, "find new ways to make it even cooler."

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:06.660
Holland later assured his adoring fans that
Sony would do right by Spider-Man even without

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:07.640
Marvel involved.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.640
He told GQ's Zach Baron:

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:13.790
"Sony has also been really good to me, and
the global success of Spider-Man: Far From

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:17.200
Home is a real testament to their support,
skill and commitment.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:20.740
The legacy and future of Spidey rests in Sony's
safe hands.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:22.760
I really am nothing but grateful."

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.440
See where we're going with all this?

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:29.420
Tom Holland truly is the definition of a stand-up
guy, so it should come as no surprise that

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:33.980
he went out of his way to get in touch with
Disney's Bob Iger and Sony's Tom Rothman to

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:38.590
figure out a way to end the fighting, get
fans to smile again, and bring fat stacks

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:44.140
of cash to both studios' bank accounts with
a third Spider-Man movie and another MCU collaboration.

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:49.000
With great power comes great responsibility,
and Holland used his for good — just like

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.000
Spider-Man would.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:57.491
"When you can do the things that I can, but
you don't, and then the bad things happen...

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.120
they happen because of you."

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:03.740
Fans can catch Holland back in the Spidey
suit for the yet-untitled third Spider-Man

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:07.680
film, set to launch in theaters on July 16,
2021.

